{"event":"changes_requested","job_id":"docs-point-of-sale-user-manuals-p630-user-manual","reason":"The full pinned raw was independently read and its SHA-256 and five quote locators match. The P630 physical-terminal identity, 30.5 cm deactivator clearance, store/synchronization timing, network and power setup, disabled menu icons, passcodes, local totals, kiosk default, airplane-mode prerequisite, and dated-evidence boundary are supported. The primary payment-terminal reciprocal route and narrow secondary Android-terminal route are relevant. One central first-use inspection step is missing from the otherwise checklist-like takeaway and fixed query answer: when Customer Area access is available, the raw also instructs the operator to use the order's track-and-trace link to verify that the carrier confirms delivery (line 61). A reader asking what must be checked before first use could treat the current visible list as complete and skip that delivery verification; a raw locator alone does not repair that direct checklist answer."}
