{"event":"changes_requested","job_id":"docs-point-of-sale-user-manuals-p400-plus-user-manual","reason":"Full pinned raw independently read; SHA-256 and all five quote locators match. The candidate correctly preserves the dated Brazil new-order exception and April 2029 repair statement, conditional camlock, severe wrong-cable/RS232 damage warning, store boarding and synchronization timing, scoped connection tests, passcodes and software-version menu qualifier. The payment-terminal hub is the right primary reciprocal route. One security-inspection step is absent from the candidate's direct before-use checklist and the second fixed query answer: when Customer Area access is available, the operator must use the order's track-and-trace link to verify that the carrier confirms delivery (raw lines 72\u201375). Because those passages purport to answer which checks precede use, a reader could skip this provenance check; the generic raw locator does not repair the immediate checklist. The fixed answer also says inspect for 'interference' where the manual says inspect for physical tampering (lines 68\u201381). Totals reset is a routine menu-table detail with a raw locator and is not a separate blocker."}
